Not shipped to consumers, by decision rather than by omission.

`v0.32.0` deliberately RETIRED the pointer that named this file (`steps/retro.md`,
then `SKILL.md`); its own verification line was `grep -rn research-citations core/`
-> 0 hits. The file was reintroduced later as reference prose and never rewired, so
nothing in the shipped rulebook points at it.

It stayed in `audit-rule-files.sh`'s IN_SCOPE regex the whole time. IN_SCOPE is the
set of paths a POINTER may resolve against, so an alternand naming a file no consumer
has is a target that can never resolve there -- a check that cannot fire, reading
exactly like one that passed. The alternand is removed with this marker.

To revive: delete this marker, restore a pointer from a shipped rule file, and add
the alternand back. I76 will then require it in `core_manifest:` as well.
